title: Customized Wikitext Lists
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Wrapping a `<$list>` widget in a `<ul>` so it renders as a real HTML list is a recurring pattern. Custom-markup makes it readable. As elsewhere, you have two ways: ''marker tiddlers'' (canonical) or an inline ''pragma'' (escape hatch).

!! Goal

Take a filter and a list-item template, and render an actual HTML `<ul>` from them:

```
<ul>
  <li> Title A - Body A </li>
  <li> Title B - Body B </li>
</ul>
```

!! Option 1: marker tiddlers (canonical, vocabulary-engine)

vocab/lists is a ''catalogue of named list views''. The outer wrapper is one marker; each named view is its own inline `<$list>` marker baking a useful filter. Add more markers per use case (recent edits, by-tag-task, etc.).

|! Field |! `LIST` (wrapper) |! `SHORTCUTS` (view) |! `MARKERS` (view) |! `VOCABS` (view) |
|`open` |`LIST` |`SHORTCUTS` |`MARKERS` |`VOCABS` |
|`kind` |`word` |`word` |`word` |`word` |
|`mode` |`block` |`inline` |`inline` |`inline` |
|`element` |`ul` |`$list` |`$list` |`$list` |
|`attributes` |(none) |filter for `$:/config/shortcuts/*` |filter for `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker` |filter for `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary` |

Tag each marker with `vocab/lists`, add a meta tiddler `vocab/lists` tagged <<tag $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary>> with `marker-tag: vocab/lists`, and activate:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Lists
```

Then use any named view inside `LIST`. The inline `$list` marker's body is the per-item template (a literal `<li>...</li>` works because inline-mode keeps the body inline):

```
LIST MARKERS <li> {{!!caption}} - <code>{{!!open}}</code> </li>
```

Why split wrapper from view? `LIST` is the reusable container. Each named view bakes a specific filter into its marker so it can be reused unchanged across many tiddlers. The set grows organically as new useful views are added. For one-off filters that don't deserve a permanent view, use the pragma form below.

!! Option 2: inline pragma (escape hatch)

The pragma form binds the same configuration to one tiddler. It also supports `_use` to alias one pragma to another, which is convenient when iterating:

```
\custom tick="list" _element="ul" _mode=block
\custom tick="shortcuts" _element="$list" filter="[all[shadows+tiddlers]prefix[$:/config/shortcuts]has:field[tags]]"

´list ´shortcuts <li> {{!!title}} - {{!!text}} </li>
```

Or, pull the pragma definitions in from another tiddler with `\importcustom`:

```
\importcustom [[Keyboard Shortcuts]]
\custom tick=list-pragma _use=list _debug="pragma"
\custom tick=shortcut-pragma _use=shortcuts _debug="pragmaOnly"

´list-pragma ´shortcut-pragma
---

´list ´shortcuts <li> {{!!title}} - {{!!text}} </li>
```

See [[Pragma - importcustom]] and the definitions in [[Keyboard Shortcuts]] for the imported source.

A worked example lives at [[Example - LIST word marker]].

!! When to use which

* Marker tiddlers: the wrapper is something you want available wiki-wide, opt-in per tiddler via the type field.
* Pragmas: one-off in a single tiddler, or while prototyping a class chain before promoting it to a marker tiddler.

See [[Vocabulary Engine]] for the marker-field schema and [[Custom Markup Definition]] for the full pragma parameter list.
